  abstract = {The existence of \$d\textasciicircum 2\$ pairwise equiangular complex lines [equivalently, a symmetric informationally complete positive operator-valued measure (SIC-POVM)] in \$d\$-dimensional Hilbert space is known only for finitely many dimensions \$d\$. We prove that, if there exists a set of real units in a certain ray class field (depending on \$d\$) satisfying certain algebraic properties, a SIC-POVM exists, when \$d\$ is an odd prime congruent to 2 modulo 3. We give an explicit analytic formula that we expect to yield such a set of units. Our construction uses values of derivatives of zeta functions at \$s=0\$ and is closely connected to the Stark conjectures over real quadratic fields. We verify numerically that our construction yields SIC-POVMs in dimensions 5, 11, 17, and 23, and we give the first exact SIC-POVM in dimension 23.},
